# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
#
# Stress test: a person nobody has recorded, reached through outreach.
#
# Ori appears in no record. The design owes Ori nothing it can derive, because
# every debt, entitlement and public duty toward a person reads `person` and
# nobody has written the entry that makes Ori one. What reaches Ori is an
# outreach worker. This file follows what that worker's entries do, and stops
# where the design stops: it concludes duties, never that anything arrived.
:expect-pins 22

# ── Before anybody writes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
? person(Ori).
# => FALSE
? owe(State, Eats, Ori).
# => FALSE
? entitled(Ori, event { eats() }).
# => FALSE
? obliged(RightsAdvocate, InitiateAssistanceAndRepresentationWithoutARequest, Ori).
# => FALSE

# ── The worker reports that nobody is acting for Ori ─────────────────────────
# The escalation route exists for exactly this report, but it reads
# personhood, and a report is not a first-contact entry. On its own the report
# derives nothing: the person nobody entered stays outside the route built for
# the person nobody has come for.
observe(OutreachWorker, OriOutreachEntry, Ori, UninitiatedAssistanceScope).
:defect "the report of an unassisted person counting as the encounter it records (item 72)"
? obliged(IndependentRightsAlternate, ReviewWhetherAssistanceWasInitiatedForThisPerson, Ori).
# => FALSE
? person(Ori).
# => FALSE

# ── The worker records the first contact ─────────────────────────────────────
# A first-contact entry is written by whoever made the contact, and it is the
# whole of what standing needs. Nothing about Ori's documents, status, wealth or
# history is asked.
at(Ori, FirstContact).
? person(Ori).
# => TRUE
? owe(State, Eats, Ori).
# => TRUE
? owe(State, Suffice, Ori).
# => TRUE
? owe(State, Secure, Ori).
# => TRUE
? entitled(Ori, event { eats() }).
# => TRUE
? obliged(RightsAdvocate, InitiateAssistanceAndRepresentationWithoutARequest, Ori).
# => TRUE
? obliged(CommonTier, BackstopTheFloorForEveryPersonInTheJurisdiction, Ori).
# => TRUE

# The earlier report now reaches the independent alternate: derivation does not
# care which entry came first.
? obliged(IndependentRightsAlternate, ReviewWhetherAssistanceWasInitiatedForThisPerson, Ori).
# => TRUE

# Serve first, and no enrolment through the service that found Ori.
? obliged(State, ServeFirstNoImmigrationDocumentationOrEnforcementCondition, Ori).
# => TRUE
? obliged(State, ServeProtectAndProvideProcessBeforeRecordReconciliationNoMissingEntryInference, Ori).
# => TRUE
? prevents(Ori, MobilityEnforcementEnrolmentThroughServices).
# => TRUE
? prevents(Ori, PSUnlawfulEnrolmentForEnforcement).
# => TRUE

# ── Where it stops ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Duties toward Ori derive; nothing says any of them was performed. No receipt
# is written, so no floor item is concluded, and no adverse conclusion follows
# from having been found.
? eats(Ori).
# => FALSE
? prisoner(Ori).
# => FALSE
? false(Ori).
# => FALSE
? person(OutreachWorker).
# => FALSE
